            <ArticleTitle>GluK1 antagonists from 6-(carboxy)phenyl decahydroisoquinoline derivatives. SAR and evaluation of a prodrug strategy for oral efficacy in pain models.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6459-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2013.09.046</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(13)01120-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The synthesis and structure-activity relationship of decahydroisoquinoline derivatives with various benzoic acid substitutions as GluK1 antagonists are described. Potent and selective antagonists were selected for a tailored prodrug approach in order to facilitate the evaluation of the new compounds in pain models after oral administration. Several diester prodrugs allowed for acceptable amino acid exposure and moderate efficacy in vivo.</AbstractText>
